  "description": "AGSC-09-93 with AGSC-00-21: a discovery document whose `agsc-spec-version` has the reader's MAJOR and a newer MINOR may use a relation this version does not define; a 1.0 reader ignores it, with the warning AGSC-E506 naming the newer version, and never reports it as AGSC-E209 or AGSC-E202. Another MAJOR has no such tolerance. Derivation, case by case, each document otherwise a complete public Level-2 document (the six bundle facts on the anchor's `describedby` link, the ledger link with its head, and a `digest` on every link, the `rel#brief` link included, so no reader can report a missing digest; digests are not recomputed in this case). (1) `newer-minor`: `agsc-spec-version` is `1.1.0` and the document carries one link under `https://w3id.org/agentic-system-core/rel#brief`, which AGSC-06-10 does not list: the document is valid, with exactly one finding, the warning AGSC-E506. (2) `other-major`: the same document declaring `2.0.0`: the unknown relation is the error AGSC-E209, so the document is invalid, and it is the only finding — a 1.x reader cannot know what a later MAJOR defines, so it judges no attribute of that document against AGSC-00-23 (no AGSC-E210 for `agsc-bundle-version`, which this version defines from MAJOR 1). The reader in both cases is a 1.0 reader.",
